lesson: 104
title: Comparing a half with a smaller part
stars: 0
explain: A half of a set is the biggest of these parts: a half of 12 is 6, a third of 12 is 4, a fourth of 12 is 3.
explain: To compare, find each part and subtract the smaller from the bigger: a half of 12 is 6 − 4 = 2 more than a third of 12.
vars: a=name b=name c=name t=thing p=3..6 n=6..60
need: n % 2 == 0
need: n % p == 0
answer: n / 2 - n / p
exercise: How many more is a half of {n} {t} than one {p.ordwords} of {n} {t}?
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}. {a.He} gives a half of them to {b} and one {p.ordwords} of them to {c}. How many more {t} does {b} get than {c}?
